rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:00:29-08:00","id":1185313,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> , Amazing job updating the First Post!!! This thread is an awesome resource!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T15:06:50-08:00","id":1186088,"title":"","content":"Going to add this to my document a bit later (running a Changeling game) but a 1 point Hollow bonus that requires Hob Alarm for Traveler's Freeholds... basically there's a set but potentially mobile entrance because the Hollow is moved by the Hobs. Basically it's so you can have a symbiotic Goblin Market with a mobile Hollow set up for both changelings and some hobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T07:19:50-07:00","id":1197963,"title":"","content":"I posted this about a year ago in a different thread, but would love to get some more opinions on it now that the kickstarter has been released. Please let me know if you would rather me paste individual components rather than a link to the document. This is for a freehold in St. Augustine, Florida, in the United States.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nm5jHFk9h_-mebBuiOw-J4zQzABfyXCYjJNlgwQigAA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nm5jHFk9h_-mebBuiOw-J4zQzABfyXCYjJNlgwQigAA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nm5jHFk9h_-mebBuiOw-J4zQzABfyXCYjJNlgwQigAA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nm5jHFk9h_-mebBuiOw-J4zQzABfyXCYjJNlgwQigAA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:03:00-07:00","id":1240020,"title":"","content":"So i am writing up a Changeling the Lost second edition setting, set in the small city of Harstad, Norway and the surrounding area. For that setting, I thought it would be cool to design two courts to serve as the locally established freehold. The current idea that I have are for the two courts to be as follows:<br /> <br /> The Court of Love: This court unlike spring doesn't focus on the desires surrounding love, but more on the attachment itself. Love for them is everything from romantic love to the love of a good workout or a family member. Their way of coping with their durance is focusing on building relationships and attachments to things and people in their life. They also are very much culturally inclined in fostering love that other people are feeling((or should feel in their opinion)). This can make some of them really annoying matchmakers that would even make Aphrodite groan, or they can almost like be a traveling band of cheerleaders who actively help people become friends or pursue their dreams. <br /> <br /> The Court of Hate: The Court of Hate on the other hand have little interest in &quot;coping&quot; or &quot;moving on&quot; from their durance. They want revenge first and foremost, they aren't happy with just protecting their freehold or sending out armies to fight against the Gentry in the Hedge. Hate is cold and slow compared to the immediate explosion that is wrath, the members of this court want to hit the Gentry where it hurts. So in a lot of ways the members of this court act more as spies, saboteurs and schemers as opposed to being warriors. Their hate is everlasting and their emnity will never die. This hate even extends to other enemies of their court.<br /> <br /> So what i wanted some help with was threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. Help with Designing their Mantels<br /> <br /> 2. Find out how these two courts share/transition their power between the two of them<br /> <br /> 3. Come up with Court Contracts<br /> <br /> Ideas for helping to develop these two courts is also helpful, i have been considering adding in a third court to represent the middle so to speak: The Court of Indifference...But i wanted you guyses take on that before proceeding <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T18:01:52-07:00","id":1341188,"title":"","content":"These guys are mostly NPCs, unless you're in a really strange game, but I'm rather proud of this, so here it is<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Freehold of the Crashing Waves</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A mobile freehold, acting as privateers, coming in like a storm, snatching changelings, tokens, esoteric valuables, symbolically powerful mortals, and even other supernatural beings. They divide power like any other freehold, with each court fulfilling a specific function.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><u>Court of Sea</u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Signature Emotion:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Curiosity </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u>The Sailors are the eyes of the privateers, scouting and searching for their next base of operation. They govern the freehold's movements, guiding them past the snares and dangers of the hedge, leading them to their next base camp.</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Harvest:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> they get a glamour when they let their curiosity get the better of them.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mien:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> they appear weathered by travel, and smell of sea spray</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Patrons:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> their patron is Sea, specifically Sea as a patron of exploration </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Ascension to Rulership:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> when the time comes to move on, an old tricorn hat is placed on the kings head, and he leads them on their way.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Give and Take: </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mantle:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>*</b>Ignore the Goblin Debt Cost of the Mantle Mask Contract.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>**</b>Become inured a Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">***Gain +2 to all rolls made to navigate the hedge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">****Become inured to a second Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">*****Reroll a failed Hedge navigation check</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><u>Court of Sand</u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Signature Emotion:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Satisfaction</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u>The Dealers are the rulers of the freehold at rest, setting up both their real world and hedge accommodations while they set up their temporary bases. They also are in charge of selling the freehold's stolen goods and loaning them out as mercenary fighters.</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Harvest:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> whenever you make someone happy with a deal that ultimately hurts them, gain a glamour</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mien:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> they track phantom sand behind them, and the sound of clinking coins follow them.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Patrons:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> they are patroned by Market itself, not any specific market, but the idea of them.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Ascension to Rulership:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> when the freehold strikes semi-permanent camp, an ornate coat alights on the rulers shoulders.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Give and Take: </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mantle:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>*</b>Ignore the Goblin Debt Cost of the Mantle Mask Contract.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>**</b>Become inured a Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">***Gain the Market Sense and Brownie's Boon merits</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">****Become inured to a second Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">*****Gain 3 dots of the fast talking style</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><u>Court of Sabres</u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Signature Emotion:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Terror</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u>The Buccaneers take over in battle, warriors and thieves, they endeavor to either attack with no warning whatsoever, or to inspire pure terror in their enemies beforehand. They are the most wild of the courts and have the highest turnover rate as well.</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Harvest:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> when someone refuses to challenge you because they fear you, gain a glamour</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mien:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> they grow tattoos as they grow in power, their scars also stand out in sharper relief.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Patrons:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> They are patroned by Terror, who grows fat on the fear they inspire</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Ascension to Rulership:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Give and Take: </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Mantle:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>*</b>Ignore the Goblin Debt Cost of the Mantle Mask Contract.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>**</b>Become inured a Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">***Gain 9-again on intimidate checks</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">****Become inured to a second Clarity trigger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">*****Gain 3 dots of the fighting style merit of your choice</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25698-khalshaza456","name":"Khalshaza456","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T17:22:04-07:00","id":1376334,"title":"","content":"Bumping this to mention that Oak, Ash, and Thorn adding new Courtless organizations of changelings that are still empowered by Bargains and Mantles: free companies, traveling bands, and lost dynasties,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}